          "title": "Klingon (tlhIngan Hol) Big Number Roots",
          "revealMs": 5000,
          "rollup": true,
          "notes": [
            "tlh / lesson-5 — Klingon Big Number Roots (5 place words x digits 1-9 = 45 cards)",
            "Place words, each joined to its digit as one word: vatlh (hundred), SaD (thousand), netlh (ten thousand),",
            "bIp (hundred thousand), 'uy' (million). SanID is an equally canon word for thousand; SaD is used throughout.",
            "Klingon has its own words for ten thousand and a hundred thousand: 20,000 is cha'netlh, not twenty + thousand.",
            "Canon has no word above a million, so there are no billion, trillion or quadrillion cards.",
            "",
            "Section starts (each comes before the card with this id):",
            "lesson-5.001: Hundreds 100-900 (vatlh)",
            "lesson-5.010: Thousands 1,000-9,000 (SaD)",
            "lesson-5.019: Ten-thousands 10,000-90,000 (netlh)",
            "lesson-5.028: Hundred-thousands 100,000-900,000 (bIp)",
            "lesson-5.037: Millions 1,000,000-9,000,000 ('uy'; note the double apostrophe in wa''uy' and cha''uy')"
          ],
